  "conclusions": [
    "Direct visible UI pairs: two self-crossing 12-star configurations show93% and61%; a simple7-star control shows81%.",
    "For the two crossed pairs, absolute signed shoelace divided by regular12-gon area gives91.068360% and35.566243%, inconsistent with the displayed integers under floor or nearest rounding.",
    "All bounded-face union, evenodd fill and nonzero winding fill give93.461586% and61.164550%; both floor and nearest return the displayed93 and61.",
    "All atomic faces have winding+1 or-1 in both crossed samples, so these screenshots cannot distinguish union/evenodd/nonzero semantics.",
    "The noncrossing7-star control gives81.100423% with regular12-gon denominator, matching81 under floor or nearest; using circle area denominator gives a different result.",
    "The evidence supports the union/fill family and excludes plain absolute shoelace for these configurations; it does not prove the general server algorithm or rounding rule."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "These are images embedded by an unofficial guide, with no verified game-build timestamp or authenticated account state. They show readable game UI but their publication does not establish present server behavior.",
    "Star ranks and lock icons are manual visual readings, preserved with source URLs and rendered PNG hashes. Geometry uses ideal regular12-circle locations; it is a candidate model, not a pixel-area measurement.",
    "No source WebP SHA is claimed because only ordinary browser rendering and viewport screenshots were retained.",
    "Two consistent crossed examples are insufficient to establish treatment of winding0 holes or winding2 overlapping regions.",
    "All three displayed integer outputs fit both floor and nearest rounding; no rounding rule is determined."
  ],
  "calculationMethod": "Split each polygon edge at all intersections, build the planar graph, walk counterclockwise bounded faces, measure signed face area and test winding. Independently check Euler's face count and winding-weighted face sum against signed shoelace. Normalize candidate areas by3 for a unit-radius regular12-gon and separately bypi for a disk.",
